Nothing beats the fresh, fragrant flavor of homemade applesauce, and the Instant Pot makes it completely effortless in under 30 minutes. High-pressure steam breaks down crisp Granny Smith apples in just 5 minutes, infusing them with warm cinnamon and brown sugar while locking in bright fruit flavor without standing over a splattering stovetop.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a28848550/instant-pot-applesauce-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

- 3 lbs Granny Smith apples (approx. 6 to 8 medium apples), peeled, cored, and cut into 1-inch chunks
- ¾ cup water (or pure apple cider for deeper flavor)
- 2 tablespoons packed light brown sugar (or pure maple syrup)
- 1 teaspoon ground cinnamon
- ¼ teaspoon kosher salt

## Instructions

1. **Prep the Apples:** Peel and core the apples, then cut them into rough 1-inch cubes. (Granny Smith gives a wonderful sweet-tart balance, but mixing them with Gala or Honeycrisp adds natural sweetness).
2. **Load the Instant Pot:** Place the chopped apples directly into the inner pot of a 6-quart Instant Pot. Pour in the ¾ cup of water or cider. Sprinkle the brown sugar, ground cinnamon, and kosher salt evenly over the fruit. Stir gently to disperse the spices.
3. **Pressure Cook on High:** Secure the Instant Pot lid and turn the pressure release handle to the **Sealing** position. Select **Pressure Cook / Manual** on **HIGH** pressure and set the cooking time to **5 minutes**. (The pot will take about 8 to 10 minutes to reach pressure before the timer starts).
4. **Natural Pressure Release:** When the 5-minute cook cycle beeps, allow the Instant Pot to naturally release pressure for 10 minutes. Afterwards, carefully turn the steam valve to the **Venting** position to vent any residual pressure. Once the floating pin drops, unlock and remove the lid.
5. **Texture to Preference:** The apples will be fork-tender and floating in fragrant spiced liquid:
   - **Chunky Homestyle Applesauce:** Press down through the cooked apples with a wire potato masher until you reach your favorite chunky consistency.
   - **Velvety Smooth Applesauce:** Insert an immersion hand blender into the pot and blend on low speed for 30 to 45 seconds until completely silky and smooth.
6. **Taste and Adjust:** Give the applesauce a taste. Depending on the natural sweetness of your apples, add an extra teaspoon of brown sugar or a squeeze of fresh lemon juice if desired. Serve warm or chilled.

## Notes

- **Yield:** Produces approximately 4 cups of applesauce (about 8 half-cup servings).
- **No Added Sugar Option:** For unsweetened applesauce, simply omit the brown sugar; sweet apples like Fuji, Gala, or Golden Delicious provide plenty of natural fructose.
- **Storage:** Keeps fresh in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days, or freeze in freezer-safe jars (leaving 1 inch headspace) for up to 3 months.
